      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During December 1936, Boadilla del Monte was the scene of a fierce three‑day battle where International Brigades defended Madrid against Franco's forces.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boadilla_del_Monte",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 19th century, Infante Don Luis commissioned architect Ventura Rodríguez to restyle the old Palace of the Two Towers in Boadilla del Monte.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boadilla_del_Monte",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1960s and 70s, Boadilla del Monte saw a boom of single‑family homes on large plots, reshaping its landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boadilla_del_Monte",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Boadilla del Monte sits 682 meters above sea level on gently sloping land dotted with holm oaks and pine trees.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
